    },
    {
      "pair": "move-quality",
      "status": "MANUALLY_VERIFIED_SAME_BRANCH_CONDITIONS_AND_RETURN_VALUES",
      "details": [
        "Both negate pre/post score for side==2 before any other test.",
        "Both return 100 immediately for post score==30000 or post score==-30000; APK writes then returns a local variable whereas H5 returns 100 directly.",
        "Both subtract exactly matching compression functions, then interpolate at loss<=0,30,60,120,180,240 with identical arithmetic.",
        "Both loss>240 branches assign score=-100*(loss-240)/240, clamp below -300, then return score; syntax differs only in comma-expression placement."
      ],
      "boundary": "Static equivalence audit only; the separate numeric oracle validates product behavior."
    }
  ],
  "actualConfig": {
    "member": "assets/res/embedRes/common_config_data.bin",
    "bytes": 1088546,
    "sha256": "3600652dcea00159b7177a2c94f63b2a31da0198022fb27dbccefccf811cfef8",
    "consumed_bytes": 999012,
    "zero_padding_bytes": 89534,
    "root_struct": "QQChessClientConfig.TConfData",
    "decoded_root_fields": 150,
    "decoded_nodes": 151177,
    "unknown_fields": []
  },
  "configConclusions": [
    "The embedded common_config_data.bin is actual JCE TConfData values, not only a schema. All 150 root fields and 151177 decoded nodes matched known fields; 89534 trailing bytes are zero padding.",
    "CommonDataModel.uNc reads analyse_result_desc, sorts maxScore ascending, chooses the first upper bound where input score <= maxScore, and randomly chooses one phrase in that row. OverAnalyseResultComponet passes the aggregate result pbc/cUb. This is a game-report phrase table, not move quality thresholds.",
    "QiJiCheckBase.Ira uses inclusive lower and upper bounds of vecJudgingScoreRange.",
    "SCQiPuShiWu 8502 feeds JY(previous,current,color), clamps negative to zero, then checks the configured [0,40]. It therefore tags move-quality scores <=40 as a chess-trace fault in this shipped client/config combination.",
    "SCDaShiWu 8001 instead feeds a side-oriented previous-current position score difference to [500,99999]. It is a distinct large-error chess-trace tag, not the same quantity as JY move score.",
    "SCWanMeiKaiJu 8004 uses Spb=5, checks exactly step 9 or 10, visits five own plies, and rejects a positive side-oriented loss outside [0,50]. This is a perfect-opening tag condition, not the whole-report opening/middlegame split.",
    "qipu_analyse_ai_ex_depth is shipped as 25. QipuReplayChessboardControl.lNc uses that setting only when aIb is true, otherwise another default; this is search depth, not a scoring threshold."
  ],
  "configLimits": [
    "This embedded fallback config cannot establish current server-hot-updated values or online server formulas.",
    "stExerciseLibConf maps and mKValueConf are empty; no exercise rating formula can be recovered from those values.",
    "stQipuLayoutConf contains an empty vQipuLayoutConf and iUpdateTime zero; it does not establish a phase boundary.",
    "No JY piecewise thresholds or report phase boundaries were identified as configuration fields in this investigation. Those require decoded code call-chain evidence collected separately by the parent and UI agent.",
    "game_analyse_tips describes position-evaluation ranges; it must not be reused as 0-100 move-quality thresholds.",
    "The Const.ts strings analyse_show_best_max_score/analyse_show_error_min_score are present, but no matching embedded map keys or use sites beyond their exports were found in the decoded main bundle; the strings alone establish no active threshold."
  ],
